  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Gradual Spacing Text\n\nLetters drift in from the left and fade up one after another, so the line seems to space itself out gradually as it appears.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 3.5 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A heading should assemble letter by letter with a sideways glide, slower and more open than a rise.\n- Short titles and taglines.\n\nAvoid when:\n- A vertical rise: use per-character-rise or bottom-up-letters.\n- Long sentences: the stagger is a tenth of a second per letter.\n\nVariables:\n- text (string): Text, default \"Gradual Spacing\"\n- stagger (number, 0.02-0.4): Stagger, default 0.1\n- duration (number, 0.1-2): Letter time, default 0.5\n- distance (number, 0-120): Distance, default 20\n- start (number, 0-5): Start, default 0.2\n- font_size (number, 12-260): Font size, default 110\n- color (color): Color, default \"#171717\"\n- font_weight (enum): Font weight, default \"700\"\n\nSource: https://github.com/karthikmudunuri/eldoraui. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Gradual Spacing Text\n\n  Letters drift in from the left and fade up one after another, so the line seems to space itself out gradually as it appears.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/karthikmudunuri/eldoraui/blob/6bb8fd211ecbdfa983f5780bead27d9f3890f20a/apps/www/registry/eldoraui/gradual-spacing-text.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) Mudunuri Bhaskara Karthikeya Varma\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"gradual-spacing-text\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"3.5\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"text\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Text\", \"description\": \"Word or short phrase.\", \"default\": \"Gradual Spacing\"},\n    {\"id\": \"stagger\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Stagger\", \"description\": \"Seconds between one letter and the next.\", \"default\": 0.1, \"min\": 0.02, \"max\": 0.4, \"step\": 0.01, \"unit\": \"s\"},\n    {\"id\": \"duration\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Letter time\", \"description\": \"Seconds each letter takes.\", \"default\": 0.5, \"min\": 0.1, \"max\": 2, \"step\": 0.05, \"unit\": \"s\"},\n    {\"id\": \"distance\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Distance\", \"description\": \"How far left of its place each letter starts. Scales with font size (72px = source).\", \"default\": 20, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 120, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"start\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Start\", \"description\": \"Seconds before the first letter.\", \"default\": 0.2, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 5, \"step\": 0.1, \"unit\": \"s\"},\n    {\"id\": \"font_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font size\", \"description\": \"Text size in pixels. The source is built for 72px type; its pixel offsets scale with this size.\", \"default\": 110, \"min\": 12, \"max\": 260, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Color\", \"description\": \"Text color.\", \"default\": \"#171717\"},\n    {\"id\": \"font_weight\", \"type\": \"enum\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font weight\", \"description\": \"Weight of the text.\", \"default\": \"700\", \"options\": [{\"value\": \"400\", \"label\": \"Regular\"}, {\"value\": \"500\", \"label\": \"Medium\"}, {\"value\": \"600\", \"label\": \"Semibold\"}, {\"value\": \"700\", \"label\": \"Bold\"}, {\"value\": \"800\", \"label\": \"Extra bold\"}]}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Gradual Spacing Text</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600;700;800&amp;display=block\" />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          color: var(--color, #171717);\n          font-family: var(--font-display, \"Geist\", system-ui, sans-serif);\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .grs-stage {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          display: flex;\n          align-items: center;\n          justify-content: center;\n        }\n        .grs-line { display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 0.055em; line-height: 1.2; letter-spacing: -0.02em; white-space: pre; text-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.12); }\n        .grs-ch { display: inline-block; opacity: 0; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"gradual-spacing-text\" data-duration=\"3.5\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"grs-clip\" class=\"grs-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"3.5\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <div id=\"grs-line\" class=\"grs-line\" role=\"img\"></div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/CustomEase.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars = window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables() : {};\n            function num(v, f, mn, mx) { var n = Number(v); return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(mx, Math.max(mn, n)) : f; }\n            function str(v, f) { return typeof v === \"string\" && v.trim() ? v : f; }\n            function pick(v, l, f) { return l.indexOf(String(v)) >= 0 ? String(v) : f; }\n            function bool(v, f) { if (typeof v === \"boolean\") return v; if (v === \"true\") return true; if (v === \"false\") return false; return f; }\n            if (typeof vars.color === \"string\" && vars.color) root.style.setProperty(\"--color\", vars.color);\n            gsap.registerPlugin(CustomEase);\n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"3.5\");\n            // Motion tweens with no easing named run easeInOut.\n            var EIO = CustomEase.create(\"grs-eio\", \"M0,0 C0.42,0 0.58,1 1,1\");\n            // Unit step response of a damped spring (semi-implicit Euler at 480 Hz), sampled once.\n            function springTable(k, c, m, dur) {\n              var dt = 1 / 480, x = 0, v = 0, out = [0];\n              for (var t = 0; t < dur; t += dt) { v += ((-k * (x - 1) - c * v) / m) * dt; x += v * dt; out.push(x); }\n              return out;\n            }\n            function springAt(tab, tau) {\n              if (tau <= 0) return 0;\n              var i = tau * 480; if (i >= tab.length - 1) return tab[tab.length - 1];\n              var j = Math.floor(i); return tab[j] + (tab[j + 1] - tab[j]) * (i - j);\n            }\n            var clock = { t: 0 };\n            function finish(tl, draw) {\n              if (draw) { tl.to(clock, { t: total, duration: total, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(clock.t); } }, 0); draw(0); }\n              if (tl.duration() < total) tl.to({}, { duration: total - tl.duration() });\n              tl.seek(0);\n              window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n              window.__timelines[\"gradual-spacing-text\"] = tl;\n            }\n\n\n            var line = document.getElementById(\"grs-line\");\n            var text = str(vars.text, \"Gradual Spacing\");\n            var size = num(vars.font_size, 72, 12, 260), f = size / 72;\nvar stg = num(vars.stagger, 0.1, 0.02, 0.4), dur = num(vars.duration, 0.5, 0.1, 2), start = num(vars.start, 0.2, 0, 5);\n            var dist = num(vars.distance, 20, 0, 120) * f;\n            line.style.fontSize = size + \"px\"; line.style.fontWeight = pick(vars.font_weight, [\"400\", \"500\", \"600\", \"700\", \"800\"], \"700\");\n            line.setAttribute(\"aria-label\", text);\n            var spans = Array.from(text).map(function (ch) { var s = document.createElement(\"span\"); s.className = \"grs-ch\"; s.textContent = ch === \" \" ? \" \" : ch; line.appendChild(s); return s; });\n            var maxW = root.clientWidth * 0.92;\n            if (line.scrollWidth > maxW) { size = size * maxW / line.scrollWidth; line.style.fontSize = size + \"px\"; dist = dist * maxW / line.scrollWidth * 1; }\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            spans.forEach(function (s, i) { tl.fromTo(s, { opacity: 0, x: -dist }, { opacity: 1, x: 0, duration: dur, ease: EIO, immediateRender: true }, start + i * stg); });\n            finish(tl, null);\n\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
 "sha256": "76d91264d3f5c772027a1914d3c5076501f4d17f9f386742bc4565a626533c44",
